# Terminal emulator preference order for xdg-terminal-exec
# The first found and valid terminal will be used
#
# Read by xdg-terminal-exec, which is what Omarchy's Super+Return binding and
# $TERMINAL both resolve to. This is the same file `omarchy default terminal`
# writes — managing it here means that command's effect is reverted by the next
# `chezmoi apply`, so switching terminals is an edit to this file.
#
# Alacritty is listed second on purpose. chezmoi writes files before it runs
# run_after scripts, so on a fresh machine this lands before ghostty is
# installed; without a fallback, Super+Return would do nothing until the
# package step finished. Alacritty ships with Omarchy, so the fallback is
# always present.
com.mitchellh.ghostty.desktop
Alacritty.desktop
